{%- comment -%}
  A bar that appears at the bottom of a phone screen once the real Add to
  cart button has scrolled away.

  Most people arriving from an ad land on a phone, read down the page, and by
  the time they have decided the button is several screens above them. This
  puts it back without duplicating the form: the button here clicks the one
  already on the page, so quantity, variant and the minimum order check all
  still apply and there is only ever one source of truth.

  Hidden until the real button leaves the top of the viewport, so it never
  covers the page while the button is still in reach.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if settings.sticky_atc and product != blank -%}
  {%- assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
  <div class="sticky-atc" data-sticky-atc hidden aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="sticky-atc__inner">
      <div class="sticky-atc__info">
        <span class="sticky-atc__title">{{ product.title | truncate: 38 }}</span>
        <span class="sticky-atc__price" data-sticky-atc-price>{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
      </div>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="btn btn--primary sticky-atc__btn"
        data-sticky-atc-button
        {% unless variant.available %}disabled aria-disabled="true"{% endunless %}
      >
        {% if variant.available %}{{ 'products.add_to_cart' | t }}{% else %}{{ 'products.sold_out' | t }}{% endif %}
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
